 See the [API reference documentation](https://docs.page/invertase/denque/api) for more examples.
 
+### Filter items
+
+Use `removeWhere` to remove matching items while preserving the order of all other items:
+
+```js
+const denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.removeWhere((value, index) => value % 2 === 0); // 2
+denque.toArray(); // [1, 3]
+```
+
+The predicate receives each initially present value and its zero-based original index in front-to-back order. All values are evaluated before the queue is changed; if the predicate throws, the queue remains unchanged.
+
