+### `removeWhere(predicate)` -> `int`
+
+Remove every item for which `predicate` returns a truthy value. The predicate is called once for each initially present item in logical front-to-back order, with the item and its zero-based original index. Remaining items retain their original order. Returns the number of removed items.
+
+All predicate calls complete before the queue is modified. If the predicate throws, the same error is propagated and the queue is left unchanged. A non-function predicate throws an `Error`, including when the queue is empty.
+
+```js
+var denque = new Denque([1, 2, 3, 4]);
+denque.removeWhere(function (value, index) {
+  return value % 2 === 0;
+}); // 2
+denque.toArray(); // [1, 3]
+```
+
+
+
